WEBVTT

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:04.210
A design studio invoices in U S D C on Solana.

00:00:04.210 --> 00:00:06.386
Its client keeps funds on Base.

00:00:06.386 --> 00:00:11.464
The studio needs a fixed amount, and someone has to check whether it arrived.

00:00:11.464 --> 00:00:15.817
SolSettle puts the invoice, routing terms, and destination receipt in one place.

00:00:16.577 --> 00:00:20.878
The merchant enters a project name, amount, due date, and Solana receiving wallet.

00:00:20.878 --> 00:00:23.857
The share link carries those terms to the client.

00:00:23.857 --> 00:00:28.820
The link is unsigned, so the client should confirm the receiving address with the
merchant.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.798
The app never asks for a wallet seed phrase.

00:00:32.558 --> 00:00:36.306
Here is a fictional two hundred fifty dollar design invoice.

00:00:36.306 --> 00:00:40.803
In the sample, the client chooses U S D C on Base.

00:00:40.803 --> 00:00:43.801
Live mode uses Aurora's exact output Swap API.

00:00:43.801 --> 00:00:48.298
It binds the amount, destination asset, recipient, source refund address and
expiry.

00:00:48.298 --> 00:00:52.795
The payer reviews a fresh quote before sending from their own wallet.

00:00:52.795 --> 00:00:55.418
The quote on this screen is simulated.

00:00:56.178 --> 00:00:58.279
Now take the underfunded path.

00:00:58.279 --> 00:01:07.102
This fictional provider record reports two hundred forty-nine U S D C deposited,
and two hundred forty-eight point nine five returned.

00:01:07.102 --> 00:01:11.304
The reconciliation function checks the original quote and refund details.

00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.405
The invoice receives zero credit.

00:01:13.405 --> 00:01:15.086
The deposit instructions close.

00:01:15.086 --> 00:01:20.128
These sample amounts demonstrate the rules, and no refund transaction was sent.

00:01:20.888 --> 00:01:25.960
For a live check, open Verify a receipt and load the public reference.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.691
These inputs identify an existing public transfer.

00:01:28.691 --> 00:01:31.422
It is separate from the example invoice.

00:01:31.422 --> 00:01:35.323
Pressing Verify asks a Solana node for the finalized transaction.

00:01:35.323 --> 00:01:37.664
This action only reads public data.

00:01:38.424 --> 00:01:40.212
The node confirms successful execution.

00:01:40.212 --> 00:01:44.859
SolSettle checks the mint, owner, transfer instructions and net change in token
balances.

00:01:44.859 --> 00:01:51.293
Here the eligible credit is exactly thirty-four point eight four two seven nine
eight U S D C.

00:01:51.293 --> 00:01:58.085
An invoice in live checkout would also need a matching success response from
Aurora for its own deposit address.

00:01:58.845 --> 00:02:03.695
Open the destination transaction to inspect the same signature in Solana Explorer.

00:02:03.695 --> 00:02:06.524
The explorer reports success and finalized confirmation.

00:02:06.524 --> 00:02:08.545
Its slot matches the receipt.

00:02:08.545 --> 00:02:12.991
This gives the merchant an independent trail for the destination amount.

00:02:13.751 --> 00:02:18.062
Raise the expected amount to thirty-five U S D C and check again.

00:02:18.062 --> 00:02:25.357
The transaction still succeeded, but the credit falls short by zero point one five
seven two zero two U S D C.

00:02:25.357 --> 00:02:28.673
SolSettle reports the difference in the expected and credited figures.

00:02:28.673 --> 00:02:30.663
The underlying transaction has not changed.

00:02:31.423 --> 00:02:37.208
Twenty-three automated checks cover quote binding, missing evidence, short
payments, refunds and duplicate signatures.

00:02:37.208 --> 00:02:43.407
This walkthrough showed simulated checkout and refund records, followed by an
actual read-only mainnet lookup.

00:02:43.407 --> 00:02:52.913
The outstanding integration milestone is a funded cross-chain payment initiated by
this project, followed to its own Solana U S D C receipt.

